# repos.conf — repos the companion auto-pulls (git push → auto-pull channel)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# COPY to `repos.conf` (gitignored) and fill in YOUR repos.
# Consumed by lib/repo-puller.sh, which runs ON the companion machine.
#
# One repo per line, pipe-separated, four fields:
#
#   <abs_repo_path>|<branch>|<post_pull_action>|<defer_check>
#
#   abs_repo_path     absolute path on the companion (SSH lands in ~, so absolute)
#   branch            branch to `git pull --ff-only`
#   post_pull_action  bash to run when HEAD actually changed. Use `noop` if the
#                     service has its own update mechanism.
#   defer_check       bash that EXITS 0 when work is in flight (skip the restart
#                     this tick, retry next tick). Empty = always safe to restart.
#
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.
#
# Example (commented — these are placeholders, not real):
# /Users/youruser/work/comms|main|noop|
# /Users/youruser/work/myworker|main|pkill -f myworker.sh|pgrep -f 'long-running-job' >/dev/null
